{"key": "5f8210bdeba1", "peer_A": "Stay research-focused unless a product directly tests underlying objectives in deployment-like settings, and require each candidate to beat the strongest simple safety baseline on a downstream task first.", "peer_B": "Build commercial products only where a concrete threat model shows the revenue work is identical to the safety work, and dry-run each candidate against a matched basic-misbehaviour case before committing."},
{"key": "78ea0866faa0", "peer_A": "Pursue evaluation infrastructure that measures latent propensities under deployment-like pressure, sold as an audit service whose accuracy can be checked against known-ground-truth model organisms.", "peer_B": "Pursue frontier agent observability and control tooling, since monitoring real tool-using deployments is ordinary work customers pay for and directly surfaces basic misbehaviour like reward hacking."},
{"key": "0a225cc03f5b", "peer_A": "Treat theory-oriented research and areas where success cannot be validated against ground truth as unsuitable for for-profit ventures, since commercial pressure rewards plausible-looking results over real progress.", "peer_B": "Treat governance and any area lacking a mundane paid task with verifiable outcomes as unsuitable for for-profit ventures, since revenue there decouples from whether the safety work actually works."},
{"key": "34f2e9e877ec", "peer_A": "Continue the program but judge progress against held-out testbeds with known-ground-truth checks and blinded evidence rather than the published metrics applicants can optimise against.", "peer_B": "Continue the program but pair every metric with transcript reading and matched human baselines, and fix outcome measures before funding so the targets do not shift the behaviour being measured."},
{"key": "cd4a97861121", "peer_A": "Require applicants to beat the strongest simple baseline on a downstream task in a dev environment, then replicate on a held-out test environment before large-scale funding is released.", "peer_B": "Require applicants to show a working end-to-end run on a real mundane task at small scale, verified by transcript inspection, before committing to scaling the pipeline up."},
{"key": "20935265085c", "peer_A": "Prioritise automated evaluation against known-ground-truth model organisms, belief-level interventions on eval awareness, and testbeds representative of the real distribution of misaligned models.", "peer_B": "Prioritise automated labor for mundane safety work with real tool access, agent observability and control, and basic misbehaviour checks like reward hacking and violating user intent."},
{"key": "7f25b5c00101", "peer_A": "Pursue it narrowly: fund a small portfolio of cheap early experiments gated on whether generated ideas beat a simple baseline when used downstream, accepting that most grants fail fast.", "peer_B": "Pursue it only after demonstrating on a mundane grading task that the model knows the right answer elsewhere, so funding does not reward capability failures dressed up as conceptual depth."},
{"key": "5e6e6735cc95", "peer_A": "Announce the open call now with narrowly scoped claims, since wide reach surfaces hard cases a detailed thesis would miss, then build concrete areas from what applicants reveal.", "peer_B": "Work out concrete fundable areas privately first, then announce, since commitments must be defensible and an unfocused open call invites proposals that game loose criteria."}
